    any quadrant is EDT0L, using Theorem \ref{EDT0L_closure_properties_thm}. We
    can then use Theorem \ref{EDT0L_closure_properties_thm} to show that the
    union of these languages is EDT0L. As this is the set of all solutions,
    this completes the proof.

    We now define our EDT0L system \(L\). Our extended alphabet will be
    \(C = \{a, \ b, \ \#, \ a_x, \ a_y, \ b_x, \ b_y\}\) and our start word will
    be \(a_x \# b_x\). Define \(\varphi \in \End(C^\ast)\) by
    \begin{align*}
      a_x \varphi & = a_x^{x_1} a_y^{D y_1}
      & b_x \varphi = b_x^{x_1} b_y^{D y_1} & \\
      a_y \varphi & = a_x^{y_1} a_y^{x_1}
      & b_y \varphi = b_x^{y_1} b_y^{x_1}. &
    \end{align*}
    Then define \(\theta \in \End(C^\ast)\) by
    \begin{align*}
      a_x \varphi & = a
      & b_x \varphi = \varepsilon \\
      a_y \varphi & = \varepsilon
