Many of the results have considered the space complexity in which the EDT0L
systems for solutions to equations can be constructed, where the input is the
size of the systems of equations, and in every case considered, this has been
shown to be in non-deterministic polynomial space. Note that an algorithm
that has non-deterministic \(\mathcal O(n)\) space complexity will have
non-deterministic \(\mathcal O(\exp(n))\) time complexity. We summarise the
results including space complexity (where \(n\) is the input length, which is
the total length of the system of equations) in
