One of the most natural questions about solving equations in groups is whether decidability or the language complexity is preserved by group constructions. In recent work of the second author a number of positive results regarding the solution sets were obtained in this direction, and they are collected in Table \ref{table:results_constructions} and expanded on in Section \ref{sec:closure}.

\begin{table}[ht]
\begin{center}

