\section{Getting the solutions in free and hyperbolic groups}

In this section we give a sketch of the algorithms producing the EDT0L description in free and in hyperbolic groups. The main algorithm we describe is that for free groups, which is then used to solve equations in torsion-free hyperbolic groups. %We focus here on free and torsion-free hyperbolic groups.
There is a similar, but more involved, reduction from hyperbolic groups with torsion to virtually free groups. Since torsion adds a significant layer of difficulty to the algorithms and arguments involved, in order to keep this survey at an accessible level, we refer the reader to \cite{DEijac} and \cite{eqns_hyp_grps} for details on the torsion case.
In the same vein, we restrict ourselves to equations in groups, and do not include inequations or constraints in our general discussion in order to keep the exposition simpler.

