codex
Implemented a locally verified Track B generator based on the paper’s Pell-equation construction (Theorem 6.4 and Lemma 6.5). It inverse-generates solutions, hides them with affine unimodular transformations, and verifies them by exact substitution. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.07825)

Key results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Exact shipping solution density: \(1/62{,}503{\).
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 1,447,610 mean exact operations.
- Compact. compact routelish: at most 166 operations over 10,000 seeds.
- Maximum answer: 23 characters, 6 estimated tokens.

Files:

- [gen_2303_07825.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.07825/gen_2303_07825.py:34)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.07825/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.07825/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.07825/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.07825/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.07825/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only unresolved requirement is STEP 4: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every bare, hinted, and placebo call. These remain correctly recorded as errors—not oracle failures—so the directory cannot yet claim a `hardened` verdict. The submission validator passes all local gates and blocks specifically on the invalid oracle evidence. A funded OpenRouter key is required to finish the hardening run.
