   252	Many of the results have considered the space complexity in which the EDT0L
   253	systems for solutions to equations can be constructed, where the input is the
   254	size of the systems of equations, and in every case considered, this has been
   255	shown to be in non-deterministic polynomial space. Note that an algorithm
   256	that has non-deterministic \(\mathcal O(n)\) space complexity will have
   257	non-deterministic \(\mathcal O(\exp(n))\) time complexity. We summarise the
   258	results including space complexity (where \(n\) is the input length, which is
   259	the total length of the system of equations) in
