   433	Using the constructions in
   434	Table~\ref{table:results_constructions}, the second author
   435	showed that solution languages to systems of equations
   436	in groups that are virtually a direct product of
   437	hyperbolic groups are EDT0L \cite{EDT0L_extensions}. As dihedral
   438	Artin groups are virtually a direct product of free groups,
   439	solutions to equations in these groups can be expressed as
   440	EDT0L languages, although the normal form is non-standard.
   441	Very recent work on the Baumslag-Solitar groups \cite{DuncanEvettsHoltRees} has
   442	shown that certain classes of equations, including multiplication tables, can
   443	be written as EDT0L languages with respect to a natural normal form. The authors
   444	of this work conjecture that not all systems of equations with respect to this
   445	normal form will have EDT0L solution languages, and thus this could be the
   446	first example of a group with decidable Diophantine problem, but non-EDT0L
   447	solution languages with respect to a natural regular normal form. These
   448	results are collected in Table~\ref{table:results_other}.
   449	
   450	When showing that solutions to systems of equations in free groups are EDT0L,
   451	the authors first reduced the problem to showing that solutions to systems of
   452	equations in free monoids with involution are EDT0L \cite{eqns_free_grps}. A similar approach was required for
   453	right-angled Artin groups, reducing the problem to trace monoids \cite{EDT0L_RAAGs}. These
   454	results for monoids are outlined in Table~\ref{table:results_monoids}.
