  1042	
  1043	  Herbst and Thomas proved that recognisable sets in a group \(G\) are always
  1044	  finite unions of cosets of a finite index normal subgroup of \(G\)
  1045	  \cite{herbst_thomas}. This is used to prove many facts about recognisable
  1046	  sets.
