  1057	  \section{EDT0L languages}
  1058	
  1059	  The original definition is due to Rozenberg
  1060	  \cite{ET0L_EDT0L_def_article}, however, the use of the rational control, which
  1061	  often makes working with EDT0L languages much easier, is due to Asveld
  1062	  \cite{Asveld1977}.
  1063	
  1064	  \begin{dfn}
  1065	    An \textit{EDT0L system} is a tuple \(\mathcal H = (\Sigma, \ C, \ \omega, \
  1066	    \mathcal{R})\), where
  1067	    \begin{enumerate}
  1068	      \item \(\Sigma\) is an alphabet, called the \textit{(terminal) alphabet};
  1069	      \item \(C\) is a finite superset of \(\Sigma\), called the
  1070	      \textit{extended alphabet} of \(\mathcal H\);
  1071	      \item \(\omega \in C^\ast\) is called the \textit{start (or seed) word};
  1072	      \item \(\mathcal{R}\) is a rational subset of
  1073	      \(\End(C^\ast)\), called the \textit{rational control} of \(\mathcal H\).
  1074	    \end{enumerate}
  1075	    The language \textit{accepted} by \(\mathcal H\) is
  1076	    \[
  1077	      L(\mathcal H) = \{\omega \phi \mid \phi \in \mathcal{R}\} \cap
  1078	      \Sigma^\ast.
  1079	    \]
  1080	    A language accepted by an EDT0L system is called an \textit{EDT0L
  1081	    language}.
  1082	
  1083	    % We use \(\mathcal{EDT}0 \mathcal{L}\) to denote the class of EDT0L
  1084	    % languages.
  1085	    % The \textit{alphabet of the rational control} is a minimal set \(B\) of
  1086	    % labels on a finite-state automaton accepting \(\mathcal R\) (with respect to
  1087	    % cardinality). We say that \(\mathcal H\) is an \textit{EPDT0L system} if \(c
  1088	    % \phi \neq \varepsilon\) for all \(c \in C\) and \(\phi \in B\).
  1089	  \end{dfn}
  1090	
  1091	  \begin{ntn}
  1092	    When defining endomorphisms of \(C^\ast\) for some extended alphabet \(C\),
  1093	    within the definition of an EDT0L system, we will usually define each
  1094	    endomorphism by where it maps each letter in \(C\). If any letter is not
  1095	    assigned an image within the definition of an endomorphism, we will say that
  1096	    it is fixed by that endomorphism.
  1097	  \end{ntn}
  1098	
  1099	  We give some examples and non-examples of EDT0L languages.
  1100	
